01:39:41,439 --> 01:39:42,691
Oh, my God!

1007
01:39:42,858 --> 01:39:45,235
Sam, where are you going?

1008
01:39:57,330 --> 01:39:58,498
Jill?

1009
01:40:21,771 --> 01:40:23,523
Are you all right?

1010
01:40:26,526 --> 01:40:28,570
You don't deserve to be!

1011
01:40:29,112 --> 01:40:31,281
What a bloody stupid thing!

1012
01:40:31,865 --> 01:40:33,742
How could you? Look at these people!

1013
01:40:33,825 --> 01:40:35,076
My God!

1014
01:40:35,869 --> 01:40:38,038
It was a bomb!

1015
01:40:38,288 --> 01:40:41,708
I should've opened it.
I sat there with it next...

1016
01:40:43,210 --> 01:40:45,378
There's your bomb, asshole!

1017
01:40:49,591 --> 01:40:52,802
A bribe for official monkeys like you.

1018
01:40:56,723 --> 01:40:58,600
Make yourself useful.

1019
01:41:05,440 --> 01:41:06,608
Here!

1020
01:41:11,905 --> 01:41:14,157
Don't touch her! She's hurt.

1021
01:41:17,494 --> 01:41:19,162
Don't touch her!

1022
01:41:22,916 --> 01:41:24,084
Stop!

1023
01:41:32,509 --> 01:41:33,802
Sam, no!

1024
01:41:47,857 --> 01:41:50,610
These helmets make your scalp itch.

1025
01:41:50,694 --> 01:41:53,655
Don't mention it.
And they make you sweat.

1026
01:41:54,114 --> 01:41:56,866
Half the time I can never see
where I'm going.

1027
01:41:56,992 --> 01:42:00,287
It's a great Niagara of perspiration
coming down.

1028
01:42:00,954 --> 01:42:04,457
I'm lucky. I've got these thick eyebrows.

1029
01:42:04,833 --> 01:42:08,044
That keeps it up
and channels it out to the ears.

1030
01:42:08,128 --> 01:42:09,129
Jill!

1031
01:42:09,212 --> 01:42:10,297
Who's he?

1032
01:42:10,380 --> 01:42:13,633
I don't know,
somebody from Information Retrieval.

1033
01:42:13,717 --> 01:42:15,969
They're always hanging around in lingerie.

1034
01:42:16,052 --> 01:42:17,137
Where is she?

1035
01:42:20,390 --> 01:42:22,183
Jill, is that you?

1036
01:42:23,018 --> 01:42:26,021
Excuse me, sir.
That is government property.

1037
01:42:31,151 --> 01:42:33,486
Jill! Answer me!

1038
01:42:35,238 --> 01:42:37,991
I'm looking for a girl with blonde hair.

1039
01:42:38,074 --> 01:42:40,493
She's medium height, green eyes.

1040
01:42:40,577 --> 01:42:43,830
I don't know, sir.
They check all that at the depot.

1041
01:42:43,913 --> 01:42:48,084
We can't allow that.
It's more than our job's worth.

1042
01:42:48,710 --> 01:42:50,587
Jill, you must be here.

1043
01:42:50,670 --> 01:42:53,923
You can fill in an application form
if you're a relative.

1044
01:42:54,049 --> 01:42:56,092
Now do stop, sir, please.

1045
01:43:03,892 --> 01:43:05,769
Sorry about that, sir.

1046
01:43:06,269 --> 01:43:07,729
Regulations.

1047
01:43:14,235 --> 01:43:16,529
This is a black eye
for the department, Lowry.

1048
01:43:16,613 --> 01:43:18,865
I don't care how you behaved at Records.

1049
01:43:18,948 --> 01:43:21,368
Informational Retrieval
is an executive branch.

1050
01:43:21,785 --> 01:43:24,371
We're proud of our reputation
and we protect it.

1051
01:43:24,454 --> 01:43:28,333
That convoy of personnel carriers
is still not accounted for!

1052
01:43:28,458 --> 01:43:31,503
I thought I told you to deal with it.
And what is this mess?

1053
01:43:31,753 --> 01:43:34,798
An empty desk is an efficient desk!
Good God!

1054
01:43:34,964 --> 01:43:38,551
Queries from Security. Searches
from Central Banking about a check.

1055
01:43:38,635 --> 01:43:42,055
Clarification notices from Accounting
about unreturned receipts!

1056
01:43:42,138 --> 01:43:45,100
- Mr. Warren, I have to find out...
- Shut up!

1057
01:43:45,475 --> 01:43:48,353
I don't know what's going on here, Lowry.

1058
01:43:49,145 --> 01:43:54,067
But don't think you can intimidate us
with your friends in high places!

1059
01:43:54,150 --> 01:43:55,652
Now shape up!

1060
01:43:59,864 --> 01:44:02,951
Lime, I have to use your computer.

1061
01:44:03,034 --> 01:44:05,495
Sorry, a bit busy at the moment.

1062
01:44:05,829 --> 01:44:09,457
You seem to have rather a lot
to get on with yourself.

1063
01:44:16,214 --> 01:44:17,257
Shit!

1064
01:44:18,341 --> 01:44:19,759
Come off it, Jack.

1065
01:44:19,843 --> 01:44:22,595
Of course you can check
to see if she's been arrested.

1066
01:44:22,679 --> 01:44:27,851
Sorry, Sam, this case has become
more complicated since last we talked.

1067
01:44:28,184 --> 01:44:31,563
But she's innocent, Jack.
She's done nothing wrong.

1068
01:44:31,688 --> 01:44:34,899
Tell that to the wives of the men
she blew up this afternoon.

1069
01:44:35,024 --> 01:44:37,026
She's not alone in all this.

1070
01:44:37,152 --> 01:44:39,112
We just had a report in that Tuttle

1071
01:44:39,195 --> 01:44:42,907
has wrecked an entire flat
and sabotaged adjacent Central Services.

1072
01:44:43,032 --> 01:44:45,452
As a matter of fact,
it looks like in your block.

1073
01:44:45,535 --> 01:44:48,705
I'd keep my eyes open if I were you. 'Bye.

1074
01:44:50,039 --> 01:44:53,793
But, Jack, you don't think Tuttle
and the girl are in league, do you?

1075
01:44:53,877 --> 01:44:57,005
I do. Everything's connected.
All along the line.

1076
01:44:57,088 --> 01:44:59,424
Cause and effect, that's the beauty of it.

1077
01:44:59,549 --> 01:45:03,261
Our job is to trace the connections
and then reveal them.

1078
01:45:05,388 --> 01:45:09,642
This whole Buttle-Tuttle confusion
was obviously planned from the inside.

1079
01:45:09,726 --> 01:45:11,394
But, Jack...

1080
01:45:12,312 --> 01:45:14,147
She's innocent, Jack.

1081
01:45:16,274 --> 01:45:19,569
- We've always been close, haven't we?
- Yes, Jack.

1082
01:45:19,736 --> 01:45:23,072
Until this all blows over,
just stay away from me.

1083
01:47:36,205 --> 01:47:37,373
It's you!

1084
01:47:37,540 --> 01:47:40,710
What's happening?

1085
01:47:41,377 --> 01:47:44,130
Your thermostat's gone, and then some.

1086
01:47:45,298 --> 01:47:47,175
What happened to my flat?

1087
01:47:47,258 --> 01:47:48,968
Hello? What?

1088
01:47:49,719 --> 01:47:51,220
It's for you, but,

1089
01:47:51,721 --> 01:47:53,473
as you don't live here anymore.

1090
01:47:53,556 --> 01:47:54,974
- What?
- Absolutely.

1091
01:47:55,058 --> 01:47:56,643
Do you know what this is?

1092
01:47:56,726 --> 01:47:59,729
This is an H2206

1093
01:48:00,104 --> 01:48:04,442
authorizing the compulsory,
temporary requisitioning of this flat

1094
01:48:04,567 --> 01:48:06,611
for our necessary repairs.

1095
01:48:10,406 --> 01:48:12,533
Don't forget your receipt!

1096
01:48:14,869 --> 01:48:17,914
I'm sorry, but I'm a bit of a stickler
for paperwork.

1097
01:48:21,834 --> 01:48:23,169
Bastards!

1098
01:48:36,307 --> 01:48:38,101
What are you doing?

1099
01:49:25,940 --> 01:49:28,067
It's getting cold in here.

1100
01:49:30,278 --> 01:49:31,487
Oh, God!

1101
01:49:32,238 --> 01:49:33,906
It smells badly.

1102
01:49:34,782 --> 01:49:37,535
It's shit! We're filling up with shit!

1103
01:49:53,801 --> 01:49:55,094
Oh, shit.

1104
01:49:57,472 --> 01:49:59,807
We're all in it together, kid.

1105
01:50:11,944 --> 01:50:14,238
Jill!

1106
01:50:19,076 --> 01:50:20,828
Are you all right?

1107
01:50:21,579 --> 01:50:25,249
- What happened to you after...
- Your face. Are you hurt?

1108
01:50:27,126 --> 01:50:28,628
No, I'm fine.

1109
01:50:32,590 --> 01:50:35,092
I've been worried sick about you.

1110
01:50:48,272 --> 01:50:51,067
- Who was that?
- That's a friend of mine.

1111
01:50:52,819 --> 01:50:54,529
Oh, God! Holy shit!

1112
01:50:54,862 --> 01:50:56,823
We better get out of here, quick. Come on.

1113
01:51:02,537 --> 01:51:04,497
Thank God! Here, take it.

1114
01:51:06,833 --> 01:51:08,459
It's not so big.

1115
01:52:00,511 --> 01:52:02,346
Are you sure this is all right?

1116
01:52:02,430 --> 01:52:03,931
Yes, certain.

1117
01:52:05,349 --> 01:52:07,727
My mother's away for Christmas.

1118
01:52:08,811 --> 01:52:11,772
She's spending it at the plastic surgeon's.

1119
01:52:14,859 --> 01:52:17,069
The wraps come off tomorrow.

1120
01:52:57,568 --> 01:53:01,322
Lock the door after me.
Don't answer the phone to anyone.

1121
01:53:01,906 --> 01:53:03,574
I won't be long.

1122
01:53:05,242 --> 01:53:07,912
- Where're you going?
- I know a way to save you.

1123
01:53:07,995 --> 01:53:10,122
Trust me. I can do it.

1124
01:53:10,206 --> 01:53:11,916
You can't go without me!

1125
01:53:47,535 --> 01:53:50,621
Excuse me, Dawson, could you
put me through to Mr. Helpmann's office?

1126
01:53:50,705 --> 01:53:54,834
I'm afraid I can't, sir. You have
to go through the proper channels.

1127
01:53:54,917 --> 01:53:57,586
And you can't tell me what
the proper channels are

1128
01:53:57,670 --> 01:54:00,423
because that's classified information.

1129
01:54:01,048 --> 01:54:05,720
I'm glad to see the Ministry's continuing
its tradition of recruiting the brightest.

1130
01:54:06,470 --> 01:54:08,180
Thank you, Dawson.

1131
01:54:15,312 --> 01:54:18,190
- Goodnight, Mr. Lime.
- Goodnight, Dawson.

1132
01:54:49,096 --> 01:54:52,850
No, no, Arthur. You're flat on the G!

1133
01:54:52,933 --> 01:54:56,562
It's your breathing.
Take a deep breath after "Noel."

1134
01:54:56,645 --> 01:54:58,606
Ready, one, two, three.

1135
01:55:10,242 --> 01:55:13,746
<i>"'Ere I am, J.H."</i>

1136
01:55:14,830 --> 01:55:16,665
<i>The ghost in the machine.</i>

1137
01:55:43,984 --> 01:55:45,486
Mr. Helpmann?

1138
01:56:23,274 --> 01:56:24,775
Mr. Helpmann?

1139
01:57:48,150 --> 01:57:49,318
Jill.

1140
01:58:41,161 --> 01:58:42,162
Who's there?

1141
01:58:51,171 --> 01:58:52,923
What do you think?

1142
01:58:53,966 --> 01:58:55,301
Is it me?

1143
01:59:01,974 --> 01:59:03,142
What?

1144
01:59:08,689 --> 01:59:10,733
You don't exist anymore.

1145
01:59:11,692 --> 01:59:13,360
I've killed you.

1146
01:59:18,157 --> 01:59:19,992
Jill Layton is dead.

1147
01:59:28,751 --> 01:59:31,086
Care for a little necrophilia?

1148
02:00:34,858 --> 02:00:36,527
Merry Christmas.

1149
02:00:50,040 --> 02:00:52,209
Something for an executive?

1150
02:01:10,561 --> 02:01:11,979
She's dead.

1151
02:01:12,396 --> 02:01:14,481
This is a friend of mine.

1152
02:01:17,234 --> 02:01:18,277
No!

1153
02:01:19,736 --> 02:01:20,863
Sam!

1154
02:01:27,786 --> 02:01:31,373
93/HKS/608, you are charged
with the following:

1155
02:01:31,457 --> 02:01:33,876
"Giving aid and comfort
to the enemies of society.

1156
02:01:33,959 --> 02:01:36,253
"Attempting to conceal a fugitive
from justice.

1157
02:01:36,336 --> 02:01:39,923
"Passing confidential documents
to unauthorized personnel.

1158
02:01:40,007 --> 02:01:43,177
"Destroying government property,
viz. several personnel carriers.

1159
02:01:43,260 --> 02:01:46,096
"Taking possession under false pretenses
of said carriers.

1160
02:01:46,180 --> 02:01:48,932
"Forging the signature
of the Head of Records.

1161
02:01:49,016 --> 02:01:52,478
"Misdirecting funds in the form
of a check to A. Buttle

1162
02:01:52,561 --> 02:01:54,354
"through unauthorized channels.

1163
02:01:54,438 --> 02:01:56,482
"Tampering with Central Services'
supply ducts.

1164
02:01:56,565 --> 02:01:59,359
"Obstructing forces of law and order.

1165
02:01:59,443 --> 02:02:01,778
"Disgracing the good name
of the government

1166
02:02:01,862 --> 02:02:04,323
"and the Department
of Information Retrieval.

1167
02:02:04,406 --> 02:02:08,202
"Disrupting the Ministry's
internal communicating system.

1168
02:02:08,952 --> 02:02:11,371
"Wasting Ministry time and paper."

1169
02:02:12,331 --> 02:02:15,834
Now, either you can plead guilty
to seven or eight of the charges

1170
02:02:15,918 --> 02:02:19,254
which will help keep costs down
within your means

1171
02:02:19,338 --> 02:02:23,592
or borrow a sum to be negotiated
from us at a very competitive rate.

1172
02:02:24,092 --> 02:02:27,262
We can offer you something
at eleven-and-a-half percent over 30 years

1173
02:02:27,346 --> 02:02:30,432
but you will have to buy insurance
to qualify for this scheme.

1174
02:02:30,641 --> 02:02:32,768
If you prefer something more specific

1175
02:02:32,851 --> 02:02:35,646
say, against electrical charges over £70...

1176
02:02:35,812 --> 02:02:38,607
All you're requested to do now
is sign this form.

1177
02:02:38,982 --> 02:02:40,567
Think carefully before you sign.

1178
02:02:40,651 --> 02:02:43,987
Thinking ahead in financial matters
is always a wise course.

1179
02:02:44,238 --> 02:02:45,531
Plead guilty.

1180
02:02:45,614 --> 02:02:47,115
It's cheaper.

1181
02:02:51,912 --> 02:02:55,123
Sam, what are we going to do with you?

1182
02:02:58,210 --> 02:02:59,711
Where's Jill?

1183
02:03:01,255 --> 02:03:03,131
I've got to find her.

1184
02:03:03,590 --> 02:03:06,510
Please, you've got to get me out of here.

1185
02:03:06,802 --> 02:03:10,514
I understand, Sam.
I know exactly how you feel

1186
02:03:10,847 --> 02:03:13,809
so I brought you a bottle of barley water.

1187
02:03:14,268 --> 02:03:16,311
Please help me.

1188
02:03:16,937 --> 02:03:20,065
I assure you,
I'm doing everything within my power.

1189
02:03:20,148 --> 02:03:23,026
But the rules of the game are laid down.

1190
02:03:23,402 --> 02:03:26,446
We all have to play by them. Even me.

1191
02:03:28,073 --> 02:03:31,702
It's all a mistake.
You've got to understand that.

1192
02:03:32,578 --> 02:03:37,249
From the Department's point of view,
there was certainly a bit of an own goal.

1193
02:03:37,332 --> 02:03:39,167
I'm not a terrorist.

1194
02:03:39,793 --> 02:03:42,671
You know that. Please get me out of here!

1195
02:03:43,171 --> 02:03:46,008
Sam, Information Retrieval is expensive.

1196
02:03:46,508 --> 02:03:49,595
You're running up an enormous bill
by not cooperating.

1197
02:03:52,014 --> 02:03:53,890
Please, Mr. Helpmann,

1198
02:03:54,850 --> 02:03:56,643
help me find Jill.

1199
02:04:02,190 --> 02:04:04,693
Sam, I think I ought to tell you.

1200
02:04:05,819 --> 02:04:09,615
I'm afraid she's upped stumps
and retired to the pavilion.

1201
02:04:12,159 --> 02:04:13,994
Thrown in the towel.

1202
02:04:15,412 --> 02:04:16,580
Dead?

1203
02:04:17,748 --> 02:04:18,874
Yes.

1204
02:04:19,666 --> 02:04:24,129
It's all a bit confusing, but it seems
she was killed resisting arrest.

1205
02:04:29,509 --> 02:04:31,887
No, it's all right. I did that.

1206
02:04:35,223 --> 02:04:38,101
The odd thing is
it appears to have happened twice.

1207
02:04:38,185 --> 02:04:40,896
A bit of a disputed call, I'm afraid.

1208
02:04:43,023 --> 02:04:44,232
Twice?

1209
02:04:45,484 --> 02:04:49,738
There you are. All I can say is
don't fall at the last fence.

1210
02:04:50,072 --> 02:04:53,241
The finish is in sight.
See you in the paddock.

1211
02:04:53,575 --> 02:04:56,161
Do cooperate. Think of your mother.

1212
02:04:56,370 --> 02:04:58,747
Good luck. Keep your eye on the ball.

1213
02:04:58,830 --> 02:05:01,917
Got to go. Can't keep the orphans waiting.

1214
02:05:11,510 --> 02:05:12,552
No!

1215
02:05:30,862 --> 02:05:34,449
Don't fight it, son. Confess. Quickly.

1216
02:05:35,784 --> 02:05:40,038
If you hold out too long,
you could jeopardize your credit rating.

1217
02:06:30,881 --> 02:06:32,007
Jack?

1218
02:06:41,141 --> 02:06:42,434
Shut up!

1219
02:06:44,853 --> 02:06:47,439
Jack, I'm innocent. Please help me.

1220
02:06:47,814 --> 02:06:49,107
Bastard!

1221
02:06:51,651 --> 02:06:54,529
Jack, this is all a mistake. Please, Jack.

1222
02:06:54,613 --> 02:06:56,406
Take that mask off.

1223
02:07:01,745 --> 02:07:03,538
You stupid bastard!

1224
02:07:05,499 --> 02:07:07,417
How could you do this to me?

1225
02:07:07,584 --> 02:07:09,169
Jack, I'm frightened.

1226
02:07:09,252 --> 02:07:11,797
How do you think I feel? You shit!

1227
02:07:11,880 --> 02:07:13,548
- Jack...
- Shut up!

1228
02:07:18,261 --> 02:07:22,474
This is a professional relationship.

1229
02:07:26,478 --> 02:07:28,021
You can't!

1230
02:07:30,273 --> 02:07:31,942
No, Jack, please!

1231
02:08:21,408 --> 02:08:22,742
You okay?

1232
02:08:22,868 --> 02:08:24,119
Tuttle!

1233
02:08:24,661 --> 02:08:26,204
Call me Harry.

1234
02:09:14,127 --> 02:09:15,462
Let's go!

1235
02:14:25,688 --> 02:14:29,484
Mr. Lowry, so pleased you could make it.

1236
02:14:29,776 --> 02:14:31,527
Right this way.

1237
02:14:36,991 --> 02:14:38,660
It's a sad loss.

1238
02:14:39,452 --> 02:14:41,621
Your mother was with her at the end.

1239
02:14:46,084 --> 02:14:49,963
Mrs. Terrain has just received
that most wonderful of gifts.

1240
02:14:51,172 --> 02:14:53,508
She came to us physically new.

1241
02:14:54,175 --> 02:14:57,387
She goes hence from us
not so physically new.

1242
02:14:57,470 --> 02:14:59,847
But the spirit never grows old.

1243
02:15:01,432 --> 02:15:02,976
Madam Lowry!

1244
02:15:07,480 --> 02:15:08,731
Mother!

1245
02:15:10,358 --> 02:15:11,567
Sam!

1246
02:15:13,444 --> 02:15:14,862
Mother?

1247
02:15:16,739 --> 02:15:18,574
Stop calling me that.

1248
02:15:20,743 --> 02:15:23,663
Mother, please!

1249
02:15:24,163 --> 02:15:26,291
Is this guy bothering you?

1250
02:15:27,500 --> 02:15:28,543
Mother!

1251
02:15:30,086 --> 02:15:33,965
Go away. This is a very sacred moment.

1252
02:18:43,821 --> 02:18:45,781
He's got away from us, Jack.

1253
02:18:45,865 --> 02:18:49,160
I'm afraid you're right, Mr. Helpmann.
He's gone.

1254
02:19:30,618 --> 02:19:34,163
<i>Tomorrow was another day</i>

1255
02:19:35,623 --> 02:19:39,544
<i>The morning found me miles away</i>

1256
02:19:40,836 --> 02:19:45,132
<i>With still a million things to say</i>

1257
